    "What is your relationship with mathematics?": "I’ve always found math practical but not deeply engaging—more like a tool for solving problems than a passion. As a vocational student, I use it for real-world applications like budgeting and basic stats, but I don’t get the thrill of abstract concepts. It’s functional, not my favorite subject.",
